  "investigation_conclusion": {
    "finding": "RapidOCR with default ONNX models does NOT support Bengali Unicode characters.",
    "root_cause": "The default bundled model dictionary covers alphanumeric Latin and CJK character sets, but lacks the Bengali Unicode block (U+0980 to U+09FF). Consequently, all Bengali words and ligatures are either skipped or transliterated as random Latin punctuation, yielding ~1.0000 CER on Bengali text.",
    "recommendation": "Do NOT claim Bengali OCR support. In future phases, deploy an external Bengali OCR engine (such as Tesseract with 'ben.traineddata' or an open Bengali CRNN/ViT model) once approved and installed."
  }
